chapter start
name: section-goal
title start
name: title-goal
Goal
title end
paragraph start
name: paragraph-the-mindmap-goal
The mind map shows the notation files in the browser as boxes,
drawn by wasm from the index served by the ecosystem server. It
always opens on the master view: every file is a box with its
title, and the links between files are drawn as connections. A
box expands by a key.
contract start
id: q575f3b
question: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
contract end
answer start
for: q575f3b
asked: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
Yes. One outcome: the notation files shown as boxes in the browser.

answer end
paragraph end
paragraph start
name: paragraph-decided-box
Decided. Every file is one box. The outline of the box is the
file, and its title is written in it. Boxes sit inside boxes,
never dots. Nothing is drawn as a point.
contract start
id: q575f3b
question: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
contract end
answer start
for: q575f3b
asked: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
No. It records a decision, not the goal.

answer end
paragraph end
paragraph start
name: paragraph-decided-open
Decided. The map never opens on one file. It opens on the
master view, which shows every file of the index as a box with
its title and the connections between them.
contract start
id: q575f3b
question: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
contract end
answer start
for: q575f3b
asked: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
No. It records a decision, not the goal.

answer end
paragraph end
paragraph start
name: paragraph-decided-expand
Decided. A box expands by a key. The key opens a short list of
options, chosen by keyboard. The keys and the options are not
designed yet. They wait until the first drawing works.
contract start
id: q575f3b
question: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
contract end
answer start
for: q575f3b
asked: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
No. It records a decision, not the goal.

answer end
paragraph end
paragraph start
name: paragraph-decided-structure
Decided. Shape builds the structure by hand. Every branch has a
master file. Layout and direction are written in the files, and
nothing arranges itself. The server, the editor and the map check
each other.
Decided. A file sets its box position with a place: x y
declaration in its title block. The index holds it as the
place field. A file without it is drawn in a wrapped row in
index order, so no file is hidden while Shape places the rest.
contract start
id: q575f3b
question: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
contract end
answer start
for: q575f3b
asked: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
No. It records a decision, not the goal.

answer end
paragraph end
paragraph start
name: paragraph-decided-loading
Decided. The index loads in parts. Only the boxes on screen plus
a margin are drawn, so scrolling stays fast. It scales to the
machine, phone now and laptop later.
contract start
id: q575f3b
question: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
contract end
